1.text:
With the $d$ points
$X_{i}=U_{i}e_{A_{i}},\;U_{i}\sim {\rm U}(-1,1),\;A_{i}\sim
{\rm Unif}\{1,\dots ,d\}$ i.i.d.,

${\mathbb E}|U|=1/2$ and on ${\cal P}_{d}=\{A_{1},\dots ,A_{d}{\rm
\;a\;permutation}\}$, ${\mathbb P}({\cal P}_{d})=d!/d^{d}$,

\begin{equation*}
V_{d}={\rm Vol}_{d}\bigl({\rm conv}\{0,X_{1},\dots ,X_{d}\}\bigr)
      =\frac{\prod_{i=1}^{d}|U_{i}|}{d!}{\bf 1}_{{\cal P}_{d}},
\qquad 
{\mathbb E}V_{d}= \frac{d!}{d^{d}}\frac{ {\mathbb E}|U|^{d}}{d!}
               =\frac{1}{(2d)^{d}}\;,
\end{equation*}
so that ${\mathbb E}V_{1}=1/2$, ${\mathbb E}V_{2}=1/16$, etc.  Put
$e_{0}={\mathbb E}\sqrt{U^{2}+V^{2}}$

\begin{equation*}
e_{0}=\int_{0}^{1}\!\!\int_{0}^{1}\!\sqrt{u^{2}+v^{2}}\,du\,dv
     =\frac{\sqrt2+\operatorname{arsinh}1}{3}
     =\frac{\sqrt2+\log\!\left(1+\sqrt2\right)}{3}
     \approx0.7651957 .
\end{equation*}
${\mathbb E}|U-V|=2/3$ and for two independent ensemble points

\begin{equation*}
\mu_{d}:={\mathbb E}\|X_{i}-X_{j}\|
       =\frac1d\frac23+\frac{d-1}{d}e_{0}
       =e_{0}-\frac{e_{0}-2/3}{d}\;,
\qquad {\mathbb E}\|0-X_{i}\|=\frac12 .
\end{equation*}
For $S_{d}=\{0,X_{1},\dots ,X_{d}\}$ the mean distance of an unordered
pair is

\begin{equation*}
{\mathbb E}M_{d}
 =\frac{d\frac12+\binom d2\mu_{d}}{\binom{d+1}{2}}
 =\frac{1+(d-1)\mu_{d}}{d+1}\;,
\end{equation*}
and with the usual normalisation $R_{d}={\mathbb E}V_{d}/{\mathbb E}M_{d}$

\begin{equation*}
R_{d}= \frac{(2d)^{-d}(d+1)}{1+(d-1)\mu_{d}},\qquad 
\mu_{d}=e_{0}-\frac{e_{0}-2/3}{d},
\end{equation*}
$R_{1}=1$.  In particular

\begin{align*}
R_{2}&=\frac{3}{16\bigl[1+\mu_{2}\bigr]}\approx0.10927,\\
R_{3}&=\frac{4}{6^{3}\bigl[1+2\mu_{3}\bigr]}\approx7.51\times10^{-3},\\
R_{4}&=\frac{5}{8^{4}\bigl[1+3\mu_{4}\bigr]}\approx3.79\times10^{-4},\\
R_{5}&\approx1.51\times10^{-5},\;\dots
\end{align*}
so that the series is essentially exhausted after $d=3$.
Hence

\begin{equation*}
S=\sum_{d\ge1}R_{d}
  =1+\frac{3}{16[1+\mu_{2}]}+\frac{4}{216[1+2\mu_{3}]}+\cdots
  \approx1.10927+0.00751+0.00038+\cdots\approx1.117\!-\!1.118,
\end{equation*}
$1.1172$ with the exact $e_{0}$ above, $R_{1}=1$ being the trivial
one-dimensional term.  The non-trivial part is $\sum_{d\ge2}R_{d}\approx
0.117$.

Remark.  On the deterministic one-point-per-axis model
${\mathbb E}{\rm Vol}_{n}=2^{-n}/n!$ and with the ensemble-only pairwise
mean ${\mathbb E}\|X_{i}-X_{j}\|=e_{0}$ the familiar closed form is

\[
\tilde R_{n}^{0}= \frac{2^{-n}}{n!\,e_{0}},\qquad
\sum_{n\ge1}\tilde R_{n}^{0}
   =\frac{3\bigl(e^{1/2}-1\bigr)}{\sqrt2+\operatorname{arsinh}1}
   \approx0.848,
\]

i.e. $\approx0.844$ for the i.i.d. union model
$\tilde R_{d}=(2d)^{-d}/\mu_{d}$, the $0.848$ value being the one most
often quoted in the literature.  The $1.117$ figure above is the same
i.i.d. union model with the mean pairwise distance of the augmented set
$S_{d}=\{0\}\cup\{X_{i}\}$ used in the denominator. ∎

